<title>USA: Intel shares plunge in opening trade.</title>
<headline>Intel shares plunge in opening trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Intel Corp plunged 20-49/64 to 143 in opening trade on Nasdaq after the company issued a warning about second quarter results.</p>
<p>Trading was very heavy at 6.6 million shares in the first 10 minutes of activity.</p>
<p>Intel, a leading maker of computer chips and a technology bellwether stock, said revenues and net income for its fiscal second quarter will fall below company's expectations due to weaker-than-expected demand, particularly in Europe.</p>
</text>
